                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d437fa38-3b84-373c-aa9d-163397a51f15",
                        "entry_id": "f266ea15-34be-3a16-904e-4009cc33a877",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A group of cats or other small felines."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "178f07ac-e3f3-4aa2-a020-fee78b299044",
                                "sense_id": "d437fa38-3b84-373c-aa9d-163397a51f15",
                                "text": "A Brooklyn friend who persists in feeding the host of creatures - including me - who appear at her door will be delighted to know that the most nonchalant recipients of her largesse may be referred to as a clowder of cats."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4801cfa0-852c-481e-be18-31de09951c42",
                                "sense_id": "d437fa38-3b84-373c-aa9d-163397a51f15",
                                "text": "Real cat fights are rare in established clowders. So instead of risking serious injury, cats resort to menace and threats."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "65629d30-fca2-46c8-809f-2664300a4e21",
                                "sense_id": "d437fa38-3b84-373c-aa9d-163397a51f15",
                                "text": "2010, The Big Bang Theory, episode “The Zazzy Substitution”\nLeonard: You’re clearly upset about Amy being gone, and you’re trying to replace her with a bunch of cats.\nSheldon: Clowder.\nLeonard: What?\nSheldon: A group of cats is a clowder. Or a glaring. It’s the kind of thing you ought to know now that we have one."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8057acb-6f4a-470b-8af1-d6a20acb42c2",
                                "sense_id": "d437fa38-3b84-373c-aa9d-163397a51f15",
                                "text": "2011, M.D. Pueppke, Fuzzy the Cat, The One and Only, “Getting on terms with the terms”\nHow ‛bout organizing a party of clowder chowder. You know, big servings of chowder for the cat clowder."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
